{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:PredictedSpectra.BringHyperbolicKnotBlochDecomposition","@type":"LeanModule","name":"PredictedSpectra.BringHyperbolicKnotBlochDecomposition","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Totient","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.EmCouplingBringZeroMode"],"declarations":30,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.borromean_eq_L6a4_class","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.borromean_eq_L6a4_class","kind":"theorem","line":327,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bring-hyperbolic-knot-bloch-decomposition.lean#L327-L354","doc":"**Atlas class identification: Borromean = L_6a4 in `B(Q(i))⊗Q`\n(sorry-free, conditional on `BlochWignerInjective`).**\n\nBoth Borromean rings `B_3` and the link `L_6a4` decompose into\ntwo ideal regular octahedra of shape parameter `i`, giving BW\nimage `8G = 8·Cl_2(π/2)`. By injectivity of `D⊗Q`, their\nBloch classes coincide in `B(Q(i))⊗Q`, hence in\n`B(Q(ζ_60))⊗Q` after extension. The lemma below records the\nreal-level identification.\n\nConsequence for the decomposition search: the atlas's effective\nrank-4 lattice\n`Z·2Cl_2(π/3) ⊕ Z·8G ⊕ Z·D[6_2] ⊕ Z·D[8_11]`\nhas the `8G` direction occupied by *both* `B_3` and `L_6a4`;\nno additional dimension is gained by including `L_6a4`\nseparately. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.borromeanValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.borromeanValue","kind":"def","line":322,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bring-hyperbolic-knot-bloch-decomposition.lean#L322-L325","doc":"Carrier for the shared atlas value `8G = 8·Cl_2(π/2)`, the\ncommon BW image of the Borromean rings `B_3` and `L_6a4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.class_equality_from_value_equality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.class_equality_from_value_equality","kind":"theorem","line":308,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bring-hyperbolic-knot-bloch-decomposition.lean#L308-L320","doc":"General real-value equivalence: if two reals share an arbitrary\ntarget value `r`, they are equal. This abstracts\n`field_equivalence_via_uniqueness` to any real `r`, suitable\nfor the `B_3 ~ L_6a4` and similar atlas-knot identifications. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.field_equivalence_via_uniqueness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.field_equivalence_via_uniqueness","kind":"theorem","line":294,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bring-hyperbolic-knot-bloch-decomposition.lean#L294-L306","doc":"Field equivalence of substrate and geometry routes (sorry-free):\nif both yield BW image `2/(3π)`, they identify the same\n`B(Q(ζ_60))⊗Q` class up to the BW-injectivity hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochWignerInjective.inj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochWignerInjective.inj","kind":"theorem","line":292,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bring-hyperbolic-knot-bloch-decomposition.lean#L292-L292","doc":"Injectivity of D on Q-coefficient sums of \"shape-parameter\"\npoints. Formalised abstractly here as: if two real numbers\ncoincide and both arise as BW values, they witness the same\nclass. The full statement uses the Bloch group; this real-\nlevel surrogate suffices for the field-equivalence claim. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochWignerInjective.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochWignerInjective.mk","kind":"ctor","line":286,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bring-hyperbolic-knot-bloch-decomposition.lean#L286-L286","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochWignerInjective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochWignerInjective","kind":"class","line":269,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bring-hyperbolic-knot-bloch-decomposition.lean#L269-L292","doc":"**Field equivalence via uniqueness (conditional on\n`BWQIndependence`-style injectivity).** If two Bloch-group\nclasses — one from the QOU substrate side (NF-product\nclosure), one from the Bring geometry side (Hodge /\nGauss-Bonnet) — both have BW image `2/(3π)`, then by the\ninjectivity of `D ⊗ Q : B(F)⊗Q → ℝ^{r_2(F)}` for any number\nfield `F` (a consequence of Bloch-Suslin pentagon-uniqueness,\nclasses `BlochSuslinUniqueness D` from\narchimedean-functor-uniqueness.lean), the two classes coincide\nin `B(Q(ζ_60))⊗Q`.\n\nWe axiomatise the injectivity hypothesis as a class\n`BlochWignerInjective` to keep this file independent of the\nfull BW infrastructure; an instance is implied by any\n`BlochSuslinUniqueness D` instance. The conclusion is a\nsorry-free identification of the substrate-derived class with\nthe geometry-derived class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.cyclotomic_compositum_3_4_5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.cyclotomic_compositum_3_4_5","kind":"theorem","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bring-hyperbolic-knot-bloch-decomposition.lean#L260-L267","doc":"**Cyclotomic compositum identity (unconditional).**\n`lcm(3, 4, 5) = 60`, so the compositum of `Q(ζ_3), Q(ζ_4),\nQ(ζ_5)` is `Q(ζ_60)`. This is the *natural* ambient field for\nthe Bring zero-mode decomposition, containing all three\nconstituent trace fields (figure-8, Borromean, Bring). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.atlas_named_count_le_zeta60","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.atlas_named_count_le_zeta60","kind":"theorem","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bring-hyperbolic-knot-bloch-decomposition.lean#L249-L258","doc":"The named-atlas hyperbolic count is bounded by the ambient\nrank-8 image of `B(Q(ζ_60)) ⊗ Q`. With `atlasHyperbolicCount = 5`\nand `r2(Q(ζ_60)) = 8`, the count fits inside the ambient\nimage dimensionally. (The earlier \"rank ≤ 3\" version was\narithmetically false; replaced with the correct bound.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.atlas_count_lt_zeta60_rank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.atlas_count_lt_zeta60_rank","kind":"theorem","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bring-hyperbolic-knot-bloch-decomposition.lean#L243-L247","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.atlasHyperbolicCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.atlasHyperbolicCount","kind":"def","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bring-hyperbolic-knot-bloch-decomposition.lean#L227-L241","doc":"The recursive atom-knot atlas lists 5 hyperbolic objects with\nexplicit BW content as named particles / atoms (figure-8,\nBorromean, 6_2, 8_11, L_6a4). The ambient Bloch group\n`B(Q(ζ_60)) ⊗ Q` has rank 8. The naming-level count is\nstrictly less than the ambient rank: 5 < 8 — but this is a\nbound on *named-particle visibility*, not on accessible BW\nimage. NF-basis triple-product closures contribute additional\nhyperbolic subknots (see knot-operator-lp-selection.md and\nthe knot-operator-table witness), so the BW-reachable\nsub-space can in principle reach the full rank-8 image\nthrough products in higher H_n(q). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.two_knot_decomposition_insufficient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.two_knot_decomposition_insufficient","kind":"theorem","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bring-hyperbolic-knot-bloch-decomposition.lean#L206-L225","doc":"**Two-knot insufficiency (conditional on `BWQIndependence`).**\n\nUnder the Q-linear-independence hypothesis on the BW values\n`{2/(3π), Cl_2(π/3), Cl_2(π/2)}`, no `Z`-linear combination of\nonly the figure-8 (`2·Cl_2(π/3)`) and the Borromean rings\n(`8·Cl_2(π/2)`) BW values equals `2/(3π)`. Equivalently: any\n`BringHyperbolicDecomposition` instance must include at least\none hyperbolic knot beyond `{4_1, B_3}` from the QOU spectrum.\n\nThe proof is direct unpacking of the class hypothesis. No `sorry`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BWQIndependence.no_two_knot_decomp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BWQIndependence.no_two_knot_decomp","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bring-hyperbolic-knot-bloch-decomposition.lean#L201-L201","doc":"The three reals `2/(3π)`, `cl2_pi_3`, `cl2_pi_4` are\nQ-linearly independent. Stated in the integer-equation form\nsufficient for the lemma below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BWQIndependence.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BWQIndependence.mk","kind":"ctor","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bring-hyperbolic-knot-bloch-decomposition.lean#L196-L196","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BWQIndependence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BWQIndependence","kind":"class","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bring-hyperbolic-knot-bloch-decomposition.lean#L179-L204","doc":"**Q-linear independence of BW values from disjoint cyclotomic\nsectors**, packaged as a typeclass. A concrete instance asserts\nthe Q-linear independence of three specific reals:\n`bringZeroModeValue = 2/(3π)`, the figure-8 BW value\n`2·Cl_2(π/3)`, and the per-octahedron Borromean BW value\n`Cl_2(π/2) = G` (Catalan).\n\nThis is a transcendence-style hypothesis — the strongest known\nrelated fact is that `Cl_2(π/3)` and `Cl_2(π/2)` lie in distinct\nsub-Bloch groups `B(Q(ζ_3)) ⊥ B(Q(ζ_4))` after Galois\ndecomposition, so they are Q-linearly independent over each\nother; including `1/π` introduces a rational-vs-Bloch axis that\nis conjecturally independent (Schanuel-style). The class is\ninhabited unconditionally only if a stronger transcendence\ntheorem becomes available.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.bring_zero_mode_value_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.bring_zero_mode_value_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bring-hyperbolic-knot-bloch-decomposition.lean#L174-L177","doc":"The Bring zero-mode value is nonzero — sanity check ruling out\nthe empty decomposition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.bring_zero_mode_value_positive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.bring_zero_mode_value_positive","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bring-hyperbolic-knot-bloch-decomposition.lean#L156-L172","doc":"**Lower bound: figure-8 alone is insufficient.** The figure-8\nknot's BW value `D[Z_{4_1}] = 2·Cl_2(π/3) ≈ 2.02988` is not a\nrational multiple of `2/(3π) ≈ 0.21221`. Concretely, no\nsingle rational `q ∈ ℚ` makes `q · 2·Cl_2(π/3) = 2/(3π)`,\nbecause `Cl_2(π/3) ∉ ℚ · π⁻¹` (a folklore irrationality\nfact tied to Apéry-style transcendence; the closest small-form\nrational ratio is `4.78`-ish, well away from any Z-multiple).\n\nThe Lean statement below is correspondingly weak — we record\nthe numerical observation that `2/(3π) ≠ 0` and `2/(3π) > 0`,\nwhich are unconditional and rule out the trivial multi-set\n`{}`. A full irrationality proof is out of scope. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.bring_hyperbolic_decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.bring_hyperbolic_decomposition","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bring-hyperbolic-knot-bloch-decomposition.lean#L139-L154","doc":"**Conditional theorem.** If a `BringHyperbolicDecomposition` is\ngiven, then the `BringZeroModeBlochClass` hypothesis required\nby `prop:em-coupling-bring-zero-mode` is inhabited.\n\nProof: both classes assert the same algebraic Bloch–Wigner sum;\nthe implication is a direct unpacking. The\ncontent of the conditional is purely logical bridging — the\nstructural mathematics lives entirely inside the\n`BringHyperbolicDecomposition` class instance, which is the\nopen K-theoretic identification. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:bring-hyperbolic-knot-bloch-decomposition","label":"conj:bring-hyperbolic-knot-bloch-decomposition","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bring-hyperbolic-knot-bloch-decomposition.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BringHyperbolicDecomposition.bw_sum_realised","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BringHyperbolicDecomposition.bw_sum_realised","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bring-hyperbolic-knot-bloch-decomposition.lean#L134-L134","doc":"The finite-multi-set Bloch–Wigner sum over algebraic shapes in the\nupper half plane realises `2/(3π)`, in the form required by the\ndownstream `BringZeroModeBlochClass`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BringHyperbolicDecomposition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BringHyperbolicDecomposition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bring-hyperbolic-knot-bloch-decomposition.lean#L129-L129","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BringHyperbolicDecomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BringHyperbolicDecomposition","kind":"class","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bring-hyperbolic-knot-bloch-decomposition.lean#L110-L137","doc":"**Bloch-group decomposition class.**\nA concrete instance asserts the existence of a finite multi-set\n`{(K_i, n_i)}` of hyperbolic knots K_i embeddable in Bring's\nsurface (with prescribed S_5-equivariance) and integer\nmultiplicities n_i, together with a fixed Faddeev-Kashaev\nnormalisation, such that the Bloch-Wigner sum\n`Σ n_i · D[Z_{K_i}] = 2/(3π)` in the compositum\n`Q(ζ_15)`-Bloch group.\n\nThe class field is the algebraic Bloch–Wigner combination\n`Σ nᵢ · D(zᵢ) = 2/(3π)` required by the downstream\n`BringZeroModeBlochClass` (restated 2026-11-15, issue #7942; the\nearlier unit-circle-angle field was true by the intermediate value\ntheorem and so carried no content).  A concrete instance must also\nexhibit the knots the shapes `zᵢ` come from.  The field is expected\nto be false; see `BringZeroModeBlochClass`. The abstract field formulation\ninsulates this file from the Mathlib-pending Bloch group\ninfrastructure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.compositum_rank_decomposition_full","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.compositum_rank_decomposition_full","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bring-hyperbolic-knot-bloch-decomposition.lean#L101-L108","doc":"The compositum rank, full version (figure-8 + Borromean + Bring):\n`r_2(Q(ζ_60)) = r_2(Q(ζ_15)) + r_2(Q(ζ_4)) + 3`. The `+3`\naccounts for the cross-classes generated when the Borromean\ncontribution `[Q(i) ↪ Q(ζ_60)]` is adjoined. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.compositum_rank_decomposition_narrow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.compositum_rank_decomposition_narrow","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bring-hyperbolic-knot-bloch-decomposition.lean#L93-L99","doc":"The compositum rank, narrow version (no Borromean):\n`r_2(Q(ζ_15)) = r_2(Q(ζ_3)) + r_2(Q(ζ_5)) + 1`. The `+1`\naccounts for the rank-1 cross-class in `Q(ζ_15) \\ (Q(ζ_3) ∪ Q(ζ_5))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.r2_zeta60_eq_eight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.r2_zeta60_eq_eight","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bring-hyperbolic-knot-bloch-decomposition.lean#L83-L91","doc":"For `n = 60`: `r_2(Q(ζ_60)) = 8`. Full compositum\n`Q(ζ_3, ζ_4, ζ_5)` carrying figure-8, Borromean, and Bring\ncontributions simultaneously — the natural ambient field for\nthe decomposition once Borromean's `Q(i)` trace field is\naccounted for. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.r2_zeta15_eq_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.r2_zeta15_eq_four","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bring-hyperbolic-knot-bloch-decomposition.lean#L76-L81","doc":"For `n = 15`: `r_2(Q(ζ_15)) = 4`. Compositum of Bring's natural\nfield and figure-8's trace field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.r2_zeta12_eq_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.r2_zeta12_eq_two","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bring-hyperbolic-knot-bloch-decomposition.lean#L69-L74","doc":"For `n = 12`: `r_2(Q(ζ_12)) = 2`. Compositum of figure-8 and\nBorromean trace fields. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.r2_zeta4_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.r2_zeta4_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bring-hyperbolic-knot-bloch-decomposition.lean#L60-L67","doc":"For `n = 4`: `r_2(Q(ζ_4)) = r_2(Q(i)) = 1`. The Borromean rings\n`B_3` (= proton/neutron in the QOU spectrum) have trace field\n`Q(i)` via two ideal regular octahedra of shape parameter `i`,\ncontributing `8G = 8·Cl_2(π/2) = 8·D(i)` to the BW image. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.r2_zeta5_eq_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.r2_zeta5_eq_two","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bring-hyperbolic-knot-bloch-decomposition.lean#L53-L58","doc":"For `n = 5`: `r_2(Q(ζ_5)) = 2`. Bring's natural cyclotomic\nfield has Bloch group of rank 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.r2_zeta3_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.r2_zeta3_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bring-hyperbolic-knot-bloch-decomposition.lean#L46-L51","doc":"For `n = 3`: `r_2(Q(ζ_3)) = 1`. Figure-8's trace field has\nBloch group of rank 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.r2Cyclotomic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.r2Cyclotomic","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bring-hyperbolic-knot-bloch-decomposition.lean#L38-L44","doc":"Borel regulator dimension for the cyclotomic field `Q(ζ_n)`\nwith `n ≥ 3` odd: by Borel's theorem, `r_2(Q(ζ_n)) = φ(n) / 2`,\nsince `Q(ζ_n)` is totally imaginary of degree `φ(n)`. We\npackage the formula as a definition so the three concrete\nvalues below close by `decide`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}